# Implementation Plan - Bond Health Clinical Criteria Engine

A full-stack, production-grade **Clinical Criteria Engine** and patient trial recruitment platform for **Bond Health**, built according to the engineering requirements, healthcare interoperability standards (FHIR R4), and AI-assisted screening workflows specified in the job description.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Tech Stack Alignment**:
> The project will be set up as a modern full-stack web application in a dedicated folder `clinical-criteria-engine` using:
> - **Frontend**: Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript, Lucide Icons, and modern clinical styling (Tailwind CSS 4 + custom design system tokens).
> - **Healthcare Data Model**: Standard HL7 FHIR R4 schema models (`Patient`, `Condition`, `Observation`, `MedicationRequest`, `Procedure`, `DocumentReference`).
> - **Clinical Evaluation Engine**: Deterministic rules engine (LOINC, ICD-10, SNOMED, RxNorm, range & temporal operators) + semantic clinical evidence extraction.
> - **AI Workflows**: Protocol parsing & criteria extraction, clinical grounding with exact EHR evidence tracing, AI-assisted recruitment SMS/email generation, and an interactive voice screening call simulator (simulating ElevenLabs/Twilio screening agent).
> - **EHR Pipeline Monitor**: Ingestion pipeline status for Epic, athenahealth, eClinicalWorks, and OncoEMR with retry logic, rate limit telemetry, and pagination tracking.

> [!NOTE]
> The engine will include rich, preloaded clinical trial protocols (e.g. *Phase III Advanced Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer with EGFR/PD-L1 biomarkers*, *Type 2 Diabetes with CKD*, and *CAR-T Relapsed DLBCL*) and a synthetic cohort of 12+ realistic FHIR R4 patients with diverse clinical histories, lab values, and progress notes to demonstrate edge cases, pass/fail evaluations, and clinician audit trails out of the box. Users can also add custom trials, criteria, and patients, or upload FHIR JSON bundles.

